Desc     A curtain wall of dressed grey stone curves away east and west from
this gap, standing three times the height of a man where it survives
and reduced to a grassy bank where it does not. Beyond it, the ruined
spires of Kaleth rise against the northern sky.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40301
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40911
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40913
Name     Uxi Trace~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A broad trampled corridor runs through the grass here, churned to mud
in the low places by something heavy and hooved travelling in numbers.
The verges are stripped bare to the root.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40914
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction southeast~
ToRoom    40901
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40903 3 40913
Reset M 0 40909 3 40913
Reset O 0 40907 1 40913
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40914
Name     Boulder Field~
Sector   hills~
Flags    ~
Desc     Ice-split boulders lie scattered across the slope, some the size of
small buildings, and the path threads between them without any
pretence of directness. Wind moans in the gaps.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40915
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40913
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40909 3 40914
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40915
Name     The Cold Stair~
Sector   mountain~
Flags    ~
Desc     The trail becomes a stair here, cut into the mountainside in shallow
risers worn concave by generations of climbing initiates. Frost
survives in the shadow of every step, even at midday.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40916
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40914
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40916
Name     Trialsgate Shelf~
Sector   mountain~
Flags    ~
Desc     The stair opens onto a narrow shelf of rock with a very long drop on
one side and the sheer face of the mountain on the other. Above and
north, the walls of Padawan Kesh grow straight out of the cliff as
though the two were never separate.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40001
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40915
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40917
Name     Westering Track~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The trail runs dead straight west across open grassland, raised
slightly on a causeway of packed earth. It is the fastest walking on
Tython and the most exposed.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40904
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40918
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40902 2 40917
Reset O 0 40905 1 40917
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40918
Name     Ak Coppice~
Sector   forest~
Flags    ~
Desc     A stand of young ak trees has been coppiced here, cut back repeatedly
to the stool so that each stump throws up a crown of straight pale
poles. The Je'daii take staves from this wood.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40917
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40919
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40901 2 40918
Reset O 0 40901 1 40918
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40919
Name     Frost Meadow~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The grass here holds frost until well after noon, silvering the whole
meadow in a way that looks like standing water from a distance. Breath
fogs even in summer.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40918
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40920
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40910 2 40919
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40920
Name     Cloudburst Foot~
Sector   hills~
Flags    ~
Desc     The Cloudburst Mountains begin without warning, the grassland simply
running up against a rampart of grey rock and stopping. A single
switchback path climbs northward into the cloud that gives the range
its name.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40921
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40919
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40911 2 40920
Reset O 0 40908 1 40920
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40921
Name     The White Corridor~
Sector   mountain~
Flags    ~
Desc     Snow lies packed hard between two walls of rock here, blue in the
depths of the drifts and blinding where the sun reaches it. Somewhere
north and above, bells are ringing in the cold.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40501
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40920
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40922
Name     Ashfall Grass~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     Fine grey ash has settled over the grassland here, dulling every
colour and lifting in slow clouds at each footfall. It tastes faintly
of metal.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40923
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction northeast~
ToRoom    40906
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40915 2 40922
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40923
Name     The Dead Wood~
Sector   forest~
Flags    ~
Desc     The ak trees here are long dead, standing bark-stripped and grey with
their branches still reaching. Nothing has fallen; there is not enough
rot in this air to bring anything down.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40922
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40924
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40905 2 40923
Reset O 0 40903 1 40923
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40924
Name     Cinder Flats~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     Black volcanic grit covers the ground in place of soil, crunching and
shifting underfoot. Heat comes up through the soles of the boots,
steady and patient.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40923
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40925
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40915 2 40924
Reset O 0 40909 1 40924
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40925
Name     The Slag Road~
Sector   hills~
Flags    ~
Desc     A road of poured and cooled slag runs west along the valley floor,
glassy black and treacherously smooth. It was built for hauling ore,
and the ruts of the sledges are still visible.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40924
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40926
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40915 2 40925
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40926
Name     Forgemouth~
Sector   hills~
Flags    ~
Desc     The air shimmers. North of here the ground opens into the caldera that
houses Vur Tepe, and the hammering carries up out of it in a slow,
unhurried rhythm that never entirely stops.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40101
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40925
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40927
Name     The Bending Grass~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The grass here grows in a permanent southward lean, as though
something beyond the horizon has been pulling at it for a very long
time. Straightened by hand, a stem will bend back within the hour.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40909
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40928
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40907 2 40927
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40928
Name     Silent Wood~
Sector   forest~
Flags    ~
Desc     Ak trees crowd close on both sides of the path, and there is no
birdsong at all. The silence is not empty; it has the quality of a
held breath.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40927
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40929
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40905 2 40928
Reset M 0 40912 4 40928
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40929
Name     The Leaning Stones~
Sector   forest~
Flags    ~
Desc     A dozen standing stones tilt at increasing angles the further south
they stand, the last of them almost flat. Whatever foundation they
were set in has been drawn slowly out from under them.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40928
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40930
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40906 2 40929
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40930
Name     Chasm Verge~
Sector   hills~
Flags    ~
Desc     The forest stops at a raw edge of rock. Beyond it the ground is simply
absent, and the far side of the Chasm is a pale line so distant it
might be weather. Warm air rises steadily out of the gap.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40929
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40931
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40906 2 40930
Reset M 0 40917 1 40930
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40931
Name     The Span Anchor~
Sector   hills~
Flags    ~
Desc     Great cables of dark alloy rise out of the bedrock here and stretch
north across the Chasm toward the impossible silhouette of Anil Kesh,
which hangs over the drop supported by nothing that can be seen from
this side.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40201
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40930
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40917 1 40931
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40932
Name     Sparse Wood~
Sector   forest~
Flags    ~
Desc     The ak trees thin and shrink as the path runs southeast, their crowns
ragged and their roots increasingly exposed above the drifting soil.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40933
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction northwest~
ToRoom    40908
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40905 2 40932
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40933
Name     The Grass Edge~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     This is the last of the grassland. It survives in coarse tufts
anchored in sand, each one holding a small mound of soil against the
wind that is patiently removing everything else.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40932
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40934
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40934
Name     Rippled Sand~
Sector   desert~
Flags    ~
Desc     Wind-carved ridges of red sand run in long parallel lines to the
horizon, each crest sharp enough to cast a shadow. Walking across them
is far harder than walking along them.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40933
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40935
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40906 2 40934
Reset M 0 40914 2 40934
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40935
Name     The Singing Dunes~
Sector   desert~
Flags    ~
Desc     Sand slides constantly down the lee faces of these dunes, and the
friction of it produces a low sustained note that rises and falls
without ever stopping. Qigong Kesh is said to have been sited here for
the sound.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40936
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40934
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40914 2 40935
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40936
Name     Windward Pan~
Sector   desert~
Flags    ~
Desc     A flat pan of hard-baked clay stretches out below the dunes, swept
clean by the wind and marked only by the landing scars of small craft.
The Temple's walls stand north across the pan.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40401
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40935
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40914 2 40936
Reset O 0 40904 1 40936
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40937
Name     The Green Tunnel~
Sector   forest~
Flags    ~
Desc     The ak canopy closes completely overhead, and the path runs east
through a long green tunnel of leaves where the light arrives already
coloured. Sound does not carry far in here.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40938
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40905
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40902 2 40937
Reset M 0 40908 3 40937
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40938
Name     Fern Hollow~
Sector   forest~
Flags    ~
Desc     The ground dips into a bowl filled shoulder-high with ferns, which
have to be waded rather than walked. Somewhere underneath them, water
is running.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40939
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40937
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40912 4 40938
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40939
Name     The Watersmeet~
Sector   forest~
Flags    ~
Desc     Two streams join here under the trees, and a footbridge of a single
squared ak trunk crosses the combined flow. A path branches away
northeast along the water's edge.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40940
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40938
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction northeast~
ToRoom    40946
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40912 4 40939
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40940
Name     Salt Wind Wood~
Sector   forest~
Flags    ~
Desc     The trees lean away from the east, all of them, permanently. The wind
that shaped them carries the smell of the sea, and the leaves have the
tough waxy look of coastal growth.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40941
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40939
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40908 3 40940
Reset M 0 40913 1 40940
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40941
Name     Masara Headland~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The wood ends on open clifftop grass above a long grey beach, with the
sea running out flat to the horizon. Bodhi's painted roofs are visible
to the north, bright against all that grey.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40601
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40940
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40942
Name     The Ordered Grove~
Sector   forest~
Flags    ~
Desc     Ak trees stand here in exact ranks, planted rather than grown wild,
each one the same distance from its neighbours as from the path. The
regularity is restful for a while and then is not.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40943
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction southwest~
ToRoom    40903
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40907 2 40942
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40943
Name     Balance Steps~
Sector   hills~
Flags    ~
Desc     Flat stones are set into the hillside in a long ascending line, each
one placed so that a walker's weight falls at its exact centre.
Stepping carelessly here is noticeably harder than stepping well.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40944
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40942
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40944
Name     The Levelled Ground~
Sector   hills~
Flags    ~
Desc     An artificially flat shelf has been cut into the hilltop, wide enough
to drill a hundred initiates and empty of everything but short grass.
The view runs unobstructed in all directions.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40945
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40943
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40911 2 40944
Reset O 0 40905 1 40944
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40945
Name     Plateau Rim~
Sector   mountain~
Flags    ~
Desc     The path ends at the rim of the high plateau, and Akar Kesh stands on
it — a single fortress of pale stone squared against the sky, with
the whole of Tython visible behind it.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40801
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40944
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40946
Name     Streamside Path~
Sector   forest~
Flags    ~
Desc     The path follows the stream northeast under overhanging trees,
crossing and recrossing it on stepping stones. The water is very clear
and very cold.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40947
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction southwest~
ToRoom    40939
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40912 4 40946
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40947
Name     The Reedbeds~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The trees fall away and the stream spreads into a broad shallow marsh
of reeds taller than a standing man. The path becomes a causeway of
laid logs, slick and shifting.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40948
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40946
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40904 3 40947
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40948
Name     Deep Lake Shore~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The reeds end at open water. The lake stretches east further than the
eye follows, grey and utterly still, and the far shore is a rumour
rather than a sight.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40949
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40947
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40904 3 40948
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40949
Name     The Descent Pier~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A pier of black stone runs out over the water and stops. Beneath it,
faintly visible through the depth, lights burn in the drowned halls of
Mahara Kesh, and a platform waits at the pier's end to carry visitors
down.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40701
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40948
#ENDEXIT

